# Fixes to the Anthropic Messages API on the CUDA server (the recipe's 0084, a backport of upstream TensorFold).
# /v1/messages/count_tokens answers 400 on a request it cannot prepare (503 at capacity), never a dropped connection
# (a lone UTF-16 surrogate makes the tokenizer raise TypeError, for one). While a tool call is held, the chat handler's
# keepalive goes out as Anthropic's own ping, so a client's idle timer never fires on a long call (Claude Code drops an
# idle stream and sends the request again). A tool_result's pictures stay inside the tool result, in order with its
# text, as a chat tool message's parts (they went after it, as separate user content). The route reads bodies up to the
# CUDA chat route's limit (96 MiB, 32 MiB before), so pictures sent as data URLs fit. mgllm, 2026-10-07.
# Tests: tests/test_9002_stream_and_count.py (CPU).

